course: dictionary
lesson: 4483
title: Harvestman, not a spider
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A harvestman is a small creature with a round body and eight very long, thin legs. Its name is a clue too: harvestmen are common in autumn, around harvest time.
explain: Many people think harvestmen are spiders, but they are not true spiders. They are arachnids, the same group as spiders and scorpions, but their body is one round piece, and they cannot spin silk or make venom.
explain: «The harvestman, or daddy longlegs, is an arachnid but not a spider.» The word or is the clue here. It tells you that daddy longlegs is another name for the same creature, so you can read on with that meaning in mind.
explain: Be careful with «daddy longlegs». In North America it means a harvestman, but in the UK people usually mean a crane fly. The sentence around the word tells you which animal is meant, so always check the words near it.
fact: A harvestman is a small creature with a round body and eight very long, thin legs.
fact: Harvestmen are arachnids, like spiders and scorpions, but they are not true spiders.
fact: Harvestmen cannot spin silk and have no venom.
fact: Harvestmen are common in autumn, around harvest time, which gave them their name.
fact: «Daddy longlegs» is another name for a harvestman in North America, but in the UK it usually means a crane fly.
exercise: «The harvestman has eight very long, thin legs.» How many legs does a harvestman have? | Ten | *Eight | Four | Six
exercise: Why is a harvestman not a true spider? | It is much bigger than a spider | *It has a one-piece round body and cannot spin silk | It has ten legs | It lives only in the sea
exercise: «The harvestman, or daddy longlegs, is an arachnid.» What does the word or tell you? | Harvestmen only live indoors | Harvestmen are a different animal from daddy longlegs | *Daddy longlegs is another name for the same creature | Daddy longlegs is a kind of fish
test: In which season are harvestmen common? | Summer | Spring | Winter | *Autumn
test: What is an arachnid? | *A group of animals that includes spiders, scorpions and harvestmen | A kind of plant | A small bird | A type of fish
exam: Which statement about harvestmen is a myth, not a fact? | They have no venom at all | *Daddy longlegs are the most venomous creature in the world, but their fangs are too short to bite | They have eight very long, thin legs | They cannot spin silk
